  "rat_excluded": "Only JS14 session 01, epoch 5, trips 55–78 (fit) and 81–89 (evaluation). Old assessment donor 80, embargo 79/90, terminal reserve 91–95, trial 0 / exploratory 1–3 and all others excluded.",
  "reuse": "Original caption study TRAIN recordings only; six evaluation R-codes used in preceding instruction assessment. Originally scored W-track 81–89 same rat, session, epoch. These are reused evaluation groups for a new target, not blinded subjects or independent animals. R031 excluded in full because public hand gallery/geometry and both instructor-study public examples come from it.",
  "sources": "No raw coordinate pooling, labels, words, event annotations, electrodes, EMG, force, animal limbs or simulated data. The R prefix identifies acquisition groups; person identity unknown.",
  "clock": "Clock in seconds since the first positive integer originating hand tick (100 ns per tick; integer subtraction before scaling), or since the original NWB trip start. Elapsed numerical equality between sources does not align them. First occurrence of each native hand reading retained only when the first occurrence is also valid, tracked and active for wrist joint 1. All source clocks monotonic. Wrist grid recording time and native motion time retained separately; errors in local relative timing measured against RGB grid. Rat only finite XY rows and strictly increasing NWB times, within strict start/stop and source camera bounds.",
  "schedule": "Every 2 seconds from source-native origin, beginning at +2 s and strictly before end; include every eligible window, never select by values, labels or outcome. Wrist end = last originating hand tick, rat end = original trip duration. On rat samples also preserve earlier protocol end margin: cutoff +0.25 +0.05 <= end –0.25. No training or sampling at unregistered cutoffs.",
  "taps_s": [
    -1,
    -0.75,
    -0.5,
    -0.25,
    0
  ],
  "nominal_future_s": 0.25,
  "max_native_age_s": 0.05,
  "max_native_gap_s": 0.1,
  "max_local_clock_discrepancy_s": 0.05,
  "duration_check": "At every tap, latest eligible unique observation at or before the requested time. No future filling/interpolation. All five history and the subsequent observed future distinct. Across history, contiguous eligible observation gaps <=.100 s; maximum discrepancy between elapsed native and elapsed export-grid time across any selected pair <=.050 s. Separate future availability test extends both checks through future; requires native future > nominal cutoff, and future query <= recorded end. Rat grid equals native, camera continuity and strict boundary checked. Ages use native seconds. Relative clock agreement cannot certify hardware latency or UTC synchronization.",
  "target": "Euclidean norm of within-recording (3D right wrist or 2D tracked rat) future minus observed anchor, both in cm. Nominal schedule +.25s, actual anchor-to-endpoint lead [.20,.30] seconds. No third rat velocity column; human metre->cm factor 100 before differencing.",
  "x": "x[N,4,5]: each history interval yields chord cm, actual native elapsed seconds, native age seconds at its terminal scheduled tap, two-step chord cm and consecutive-vector cosine. First interval last two columns 0; cosine 0 if either displacement zero. No absolute coordinates, cross-recording origin, handed axes or anatomical homology assumed.",
  "privacy": "Model may use only x, domain and TRAIN y; recording/group local for split/weighting/scoring only, times/indices audit only. Keep full sample files and all subject-level rows local. No conversation or event join. Publish aggregate scores, weights, training code and artificial demos; include CDLA text, CC BY credit/licence/version/changes at source and in release.",
  "selection_information": "The source cohort manifests, clocks, source docs, public gallery record identities, published prior protocols and earlier disclosures were available before this freeze. Neither eligible movement payloads nor newly computed assessment values were opened for this study before the freeze."
}
